<section class="wrap section narrow">
  <h1>How the board works</h1>

  <h2>Who can use it</h2>
  <p>The board is for residents of Rupert Yorkville Towers. Anyone can browse posts without an
     account. To publish a post, accept one, or send a message you need an account with your real
     name, apartment, a working mobile number and a personal email address.</p>

  <h2>Posting</h2>
  <p>Say clearly what needs doing, which apartment it's for, roughly what you'll pay (or charge),
     and whether it's a one-time job or a recurring one. A price range is fine — leave it blank if
     you're open to offers. You can edit a post while it's still open.</p>

  <h2>Accepting</h2>
  <p>When a neighbor accepts your post it's locked to the two of you and a private message thread
     opens automatically. Your email and phone number are shared with each other at that point, and
     only at that point. If plans fall through, the person who accepted can withdraw, or the poster
     can unmatch and reopen it for someone else.</p>

  <h2>Messaging</h2>
  <p>Messages live on the site so there's a record of what was agreed. Threads stay in your Messages
     tab after a job is finished.</p>

  <h2>Money and safety</h2>
  <p>Payment happens directly between neighbors — the board doesn't process money and doesn't take a
     cut. Agree on the amount in the thread before the work starts. Use your judgment about who you
     let into your apartment, and take the same care you would with any contractor. For anything
     involving building staff, packages, or access to common areas, follow building policy.</p>

  <h2>Problems</h2>
  <p>If a neighbor is misusing the board, or something isn't working, use the User Help panel at the
     bottom of every page. Calls and email are answered anytime.</p>
</section>

